@startuml
title T12-WF06 — AI Churn Monitoring Agent
start
:01 | Schedule Trigger\nrun on a configurable daily schedule.;
:02 | HTTP Request: Get Customer Cohort\nfetch active customers through NestJS.;
:03 | Split Out: Customer Items\nprocess customers individually or in bounded batches.;
:04 | HTTP Request: Get Customer Profile\nretrieve authoritative customer/account details.;
:05 | HTTP Request: Get Engagement History\nobtain available interaction recency and trend signals.;
:06 | HTTP Request: Get Follow-up/Feedback/Issue History\nfetch only available follow-up outcomes, feedback and customer issues.;
:07 | Code: Normalize Feature Snapshot\nnormalize evidence and data coverage; do not calculate the official churn score in n8n.;
:08 | HTTP Request: Evaluate Backend Churn Policy\nNestJS calculates the deterministic canonical risk score/level and persists a CustomerChurnAssessment history record.;
:09 | HTTP Request: AI Risk Explanation\nrequest an evidence-grounded explanation using the backend score; AI does not set the official score.;
:10 | HTTP Request: Save Validated Explanation\nsubmit structured explanation to NestJS, which validates and stores it against the assessment.;
if (11 | High risk and sufficient evidence?) then (yes)
  :12 | HTTP Request: Ensure CustomerTask\nask NestJS to create/reuse an idempotent CustomerTask linked to the high-risk assessment.;
else (no)
endif
stop
@enduml
